\section{Related Work}\label{sec:related}
WSN-DS covers four denial-of-service attacks on wireless sensor networks running the low-energy adaptive clustering hierarchy (LEACH) protocol \cite{heinzelman2000,almomani2016}. CICIoT2023 contains 33 attacks in seven categories executed against 105 IoT devices \cite{neto2023}. Edge-IIoTset was generated on an IoT and industrial IoT (IIoT) testbed and contains 14 attacks in five categories \cite{ferrag2022}.

Surveys of deep learning for intrusion detection catalog architectures, datasets, and comparisons \cite{ferrag2020}. RF \cite{breiman2001} and gradient-boosted trees in XGBoost \cite{chen2016} are standard strong baselines on tabular network features. Hybrid networks combining convolutions, long short-term memory (LSTM) \cite{hochreiter1997} in bidirectional form \cite{schuster1997}, and attention \cite{vaswani2017} are [-frequent-]{+common+} in recent IDS work, for example on wireless IoT sensor networks [-\cite{phalaagae2025}; our-]{+\cite{phalaagae2025}. Our+} hybrid model belongs to this [-family but is our own configuration,-]{+family; we configured it ourselves and did+} not [-a reproduction.-]{+reproduce that work.+}

[-Because-]{+Cross-dataset studies of network intrusion detection report large drops when a model is tested on a dataset it was not trained on \cite{dhooge2023,layeghy2022}, including macro-F1 losses of up to 30 points for federated models moved between Edge-IIoTset, CICIoT2023, and TII-SSRC-23 \cite{bilal2026}. We add a wireless sensor network dataset and compare+} each {+RF transfer score with the target's majority-class share.+}

{+Each+} network intrusion detection dataset ships with its own feature set, {+which makes+} models[-are-] hard to compare across [-datasets;-]{+datasets.+} Sarhan et al.\ address this by re-expressing datasets in a common NetFlow-based feature set \cite{sarhan2021}. Our behavioral track (Section~\ref{sec:features}) [-addresses the same obstacle by-]{+is+} a cruder [-route, hand-mapping-]{+approach that maps+} feature [-slots,-]{+slots by hand,+} and [-should be read-]{+it has not been validated+} as[-an experimental device rather than-] a[-validated-] common representation. Domain adaptation theory bounds target error by source error plus a domain divergence \cite{bendavid2010}, and {+Pan and Yang survey+} transfer learning[-is surveyed in-] \cite{pan2010}. DANN connects a domain classifier to a shared feature extractor through a gradient reversal layer, [-pushing-]{+so training pushes+} the extractor toward domain-invariant features \cite{ganin2015,ganin2016}. [-It was-]{+Ganin et al.\+} formulated {+it+} for labeled source {+data+} and unlabeled target data [-\cite{ganin2016}; our-]{+\cite{ganin2016}. Our+} DANN experiment [-differs-]{+uses labels+} from [-that setting-]{+both domains+} (Section~\ref{sec:protocol}).

